sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1 (an external API call is an effect, so it is a run), R2-R4. swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-conn-direct.yaml, docs/reference/conn.md#gateway-session-cleanup, conn.pairing_revoke chart.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 4, 14, 15, 16, 21 (no Gateway reads from the step, session to vault, one session list, no link step).
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: none · API (conn-environment-cleanup)
  %% kind: conn.gateway_sessions_revoke
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane T3 icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>API callers
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant T3 as T3 server<br/>T3 auth API
  CLI->>GW: Clean up env-beast<br/>POST …/env-beast/sessions/cleanup
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `POST /api/v1/conn/environments/env-beast/sessions/cleanup`
  %%> - syntax: the MCP tool `conn-environment-cleanup` with `environment`
  %%> Who starts it:
  %%> - the Gateway itself, when a registration of env-beast commits a new cleanup revision; a start failure keeps registration successful and the revision pending
  %%> - an operator, to retry a revision that failed
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - there is no `orbit` command, and no per-minute Swamp check of pending revisions
  Note over GW: Check the revision<br/>task #5181 · session to vault
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the `conn` extension is on; the caller's Node has an access grant to the Gateway Node
  %%> - env-beast has a cleanup revision newer than the last completed one; otherwise the answer is 204 and no task starts
  %%> - no other cleanup runs for env-beast (`operation.target_busy`); the Gateway holds one lock per server
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the T3 URL, the revision and the fixed client label `Orbit Gateway`
  %%> - pushes the current admin session to the Swamp vault as `conn-pairing-revoke-<uuid>` after commit (R3)
  %%> While it runs:
  %%> - a new registration of env-beast refuses while the environment is busy, then validates its candidate session outside the database transaction
  %%> Why a run:
  %%> - calling T3's API is an effect; the Gateway's only execution primitives are mint and sign
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-conn-direct
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); no Node is a target
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the T3 server URL, the client label, the revision and the vault key name; never the session
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5181
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the requester follows `GET /api/v1/conn/operations/5181`
  SW->>T3: Revoke old sessions<br/>subscribeAuthAccess · POST …/revoke
  %%> How:
  %%> - the typed Conn revocation child runs HTTPS from 209, with the admin session from `vault.get`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - lists the client sessions on env-beast once, selects those labelled `Orbit Gateway` that are not the current session, and revokes each
  %%> - a session already gone counts as revoked
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a failed or invalid list stops the step before any revoke; it never counts as an empty list
  %%> Keeps:
  %%> - the Gateway's current admin session and every other label
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no re-read of the Gateway or of the list before each revoke; the lock on env-beast keeps the session fixed
  alt every revoke done
    T3-->>SW: 3 sessions revoked
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - each revoke answered; the step outputs the count
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · revoked
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the count from the step; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Mark revision done<br/>cleanup_completed_version
    %%> Result:
    %%> - env-beast's cleanup revision is marked completed
    %%> - task #5181 succeeds; the Gateway's own session on env-beast keeps working
  else listing or a revoke fails
    T3--xSW: 401 or no answer
    %%> When:
    %%> - T3 refuses the admin session, cannot be reached, or answers with invalid data
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>conn.revocation_failed
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its safe `conn.*` error code
    Note over GW: Revision stays pending<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the revision stays pending; no automatic task follows; task #5181 fails
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - safe: call cleanup again, or register again; it lists the sessions again and skips those already gone
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: Read Operation #5181<br/>GET conn/operations/5181
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the requester's task status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the number of revoked sessions once the task has ended
  end
